From e5fd82654addcec5f8007f6ee3e58dc5ca29af5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Soren Outis <soren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:08:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: stateless mobile API with token auth (routes/api.php)

Adds a JSON surface at /api/mobile/* for the LSI mobile app, built so the
deployed web app is untouched:

- Personal access tokens (api_tokens table, SHA-256 stored) issued by
  POST /api/mobile/auth/login and revoked by /auth/logout. No new package:
  an auth.mobile middleware binds the token user to the request and the
  default web guard for the duration of the request, so every existing
  policy/gate/controller keeps working unchanged.
- Login reuses Fortify's credential check, the login_enabled Setting, and
  Fortify's own TOTP provider + recovery codes, so mobile and web accept
  exactly the same second factors. Rate limited (5/min per IP+email).
- Data endpoints reuse the same controller methods the web calls; actions
  that end in a redirect return JSON instead when the request comes from
  /api/mobile/* (MobileApi::isRequest). Dashboard/exam/courses/assignments/
  public profile payloads are extracted into shared builders.
- student.page.mobile mirrors the student-page availability controls with a
  JSON 423; banned users get a 403 JSON instead of the web redirect.
- Pest coverage: token lifecycle, 2FA (TOTP + recovery codes), banned
  users, exam start/save/submit flow, data endpoints, and web-route
  regression tests.
